the first thing I would do

00:00:47.550 --> 00:00:49.807
once I buy these New York Jets,

00:00:49.807 --> 00:00:51.731
I'm pointing to the stadium, by the way,

00:00:54.131 --> 00:00:57.638
is I would start a program
that would send a jersey

00:00:57.638 --> 00:01:00.730
to every six year old boy
and girl in the New York,

00:01:00.730 --> 00:01:03.988
New Jersey tri-state area
with a handwritten note

00:01:03.988 --> 00:01:05.269
from me saying thank you.

00:01:05.269 --> 00:01:07.195
Or maybe just a note
that I would sign some,

00:01:07.195 --> 00:01:08.726
because that's a big number but

00:01:08.726 --> 00:01:11.706
I wanna basically convert every
single youth into the green,

00:01:11.706 --> 00:01:14.299
not the blue, and so that
would be the number one

00:01:14.299 --> 00:01:15.887
thing I would do, start the program

00:01:15.887 --> 00:01:18.480
that I've been imagining and
dreaming about my whole life.

00:01:19.314 --> 00:01:21.570
- [Voiceover] Mahdi wants
to know, "What motivated you

00:01:21.570 --> 00:01:24.637
"to continue any project,
like Wine Library

00:01:24.637 --> 00:01:27.253
"without seeing any
significant growth prior?"

00:01:28.424 --> 00:01:30.767
- Mahdi, you know, for me,
that's a very easy answer,

00:01:30.767 --> 00:01:34.026
which is, I just believe
in my holistic purpose.

00:01:34.026 --> 00:01:37.064
I'm blown away by how
many people are crippled

00:01:37.064 --> 00:01:40.156
by one project or the other,
to me this is a net-net game.

00:01:40.156 --> 00:01:43.948
I have a very clear vision
professionally where I wanna go

00:01:43.948 --> 00:01:46.842
but overall, I just want
to be a good human being,

00:01:46.842 --> 00:01:49.572
do business the right
way, the right process,

00:01:49.572 --> 00:01:51.857
put in the right hustle
and I control that.

00:01:51.857 --> 00:01:54.171
If I don't get results, well
that means I made a wrong

00:01:54.171 --> 00:01:56.652
strategic decision, but that
doesn't cripple me either

00:01:56.652 --> 00:01:59.047
because as a net-net,
I know where I'm going.

00:01:59.047 --> 00:02:01.529
So for every one or two times I decide

00:02:01.529 --> 00:02:03.477
to get in the wrong business
or invest in the wrong thing,

00:02:03.477 --> 00:02:06.708
I'm going to figure out
a win alongside of that

00:02:06.708 --> 00:02:09.103
and that's all that really matters to me.

00:02:09.775 --> 00:02:12.477
- [Voiceover] Michael wants
to know, "As an entrepreneur

00:02:12.477 --> 00:02:14.512
"how do you feel about
government officials

00:02:14.512 --> 00:02:17.129
"picking winners, like
Wynn getting approval

00:02:17.129 --> 00:02:19.192
"for casino in Boston."

00:02:19.999 --> 00:02:22.398
- Michael, first and foremost,
I agree with you 100%.

00:02:22.398 --> 00:02:25.322
This kind of government
interface behind-the-scenes stuff

00:02:25.322 --> 00:02:28.302
happens all day long,
especially non-American.

00:02:28.302 --> 00:02:29.810
It happens in America all day long,

00:02:29.810 --> 00:02:31.591
but you start getting into
other parts of the world,

00:02:31.591 --> 00:02:33.597
there's a lot of shenanigans going on.

00:02:33.597 --> 00:02:35.214
But I'll be honest with
you, as an entrepreneur,

00:02:35.214 --> 00:02:37.441
and I've always felt
this way, don't forget,

00:02:37.441 --> 00:02:39.395
I come from a regulated industry business.

00:02:39.395 --> 00:02:41.482
The Wine Library had plenty of headaches.

00:02:41.482 --> 00:02:45.438
I just completely ignore it.

00:02:45.438 --> 00:02:49.119
I'm disinterested and
not focused on it at all.

00:02:49.119 --> 00:02:52.987
I spend all of my time,
and I mean all of it,

00:02:52.987 --> 00:02:56.781
I spend all of my time on the
things that I can control.

00:02:57.087 --> 00:02:59.650
It's why I fear the health and wellbeing

00:02:59.650 --> 00:03:02.410
of the people I love and care
for because I'm not in control

00:03:02.410 --> 00:03:04.388
but when it comes to business, even though

00:03:04.388 --> 00:03:07.449
there's a lot of back-end deals,
people not rooting for me,

00:03:07.449 --> 00:03:09.345
deals that were made for me not to win,

00:03:09.345 --> 00:03:12.158
I feel that I have the
talent and the skills

00:03:12.158 --> 00:03:13.915
to still break through.

00:03:15.255 --> 00:03:16.757
- [Voiceover] Hayley wants to know,

00:03:16.757 --> 00:03:17.980
"What is your response to brands

00:03:17.980 --> 00:03:20.433
"looking for 24/7 community management?

00:03:20.433 --> 00:03:23.612
"Is it worth the
investment, is it overkill?"

00:03:24.864 --> 00:03:26.539
- You know Hayley, I'm a big fan.

00:03:26.539 --> 00:03:28.041
I believe that everybody
that you engage with

00:03:28.041 --> 00:03:29.600
and say hello to, I believe that everybody

00:03:29.600 --> 00:03:32.083
I said thanks to or TY, over the weekend,

00:03:32.083 --> 00:03:33.949
for watching all 21 episodes of this show

00:03:33.949 --> 00:03:35.288
get affected by that.

00:03:35.288 --> 00:03:37.126
I do think the human investment matters.

00:03:37.126 --> 00:03:39.354
I do think that if brands committed more

00:03:39.354 --> 00:03:41.052
to one-on-one marketing that many of them

00:03:41.052 --> 00:03:44.009
don't think is scalable,
they would get bigger depth.

00:03:44.009 --> 00:03:46.040
We talked in the last episode
about depth and width.

00:03:46.040 --> 00:03:47.576
A lot of you responded to that.

00:03:47.576 --> 00:03:50.081
I think that community management 24/7

00:03:50.081 --> 00:03:52.476
can be valuable if you're big enough.

00:03:52.476 --> 00:03:54.621
You have to be a global
brand, you have to be a Pepsi.

00:03:54.621 --> 00:03:58.692
You have to be Toyota to really
get the value out of 24/7

00:03:58.692 --> 00:04:00.530
'cause otherwise you're
paying people to sit around

00:04:00.530 --> 00:04:01.730
and not engage with anyone.

00:04:01.730 --> 00:04:05.209
I'm not crushing it on
Twitter between 2 AM Eastern

00:04:05.209 --> 00:04:07.970
and 6AM Eastern, so I don't need anybody,

00:04:07.970 --> 00:04:10.840
which in this case is me, engaging there

00:04:10.840 --> 00:04:13.543
but if you're big enough, I believe in it.

00:04:14.992 --> 00:04:17.607
- [Voiceover] "Okay, I get
it, go native, go deep,

00:04:17.607 --> 00:04:20.171
"jab, jab, jab, jab, big right hook

00:04:20.171 --> 00:04:23.627
